# 263 (the 12 Sep 2026 standards audit, gap E4). `.agents/` and `skills-lock.json` WERE ignored, and
# that is why a fresh clone of this repo did not carry the Supabase skills the migration work reads -
# the RLS and Postgres material was present on one laptop and nowhere else, which is indistinguishable
# from a clone that has it until the moment somebody needs it. The lock file is the half that says
# WHICH version of a vendored skill is checked out, so ignoring it while tracking nothing made the
# pair unverifiable in both directions. `.claude/skills/` stays ignored on purpose: it holds symlinks
# into these two, and a symlink is a fact about this machine.

# 240 (AUDIT-v197). THE REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC and a leaked key cannot be un-leaked - scanning bots
# archive public repos within minutes and a fork survives the repo going private again. Checked
# before adding this rather than after: `git log --all --diff-filter=A -- .env` is EMPTY, so nothing
# is being hidden retroactively and no history rewrite is owed. API keys live in Vercel env vars and
# this line exists so the one careless `.env` never gets the chance.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
